Spec: Caller-bound pending permission requests

Purpose:
  Persist minimal permission requests against previously reviewed imports while leaving network authority unavailable.

Owns:
  ./PendingGrants.cs

References:
  ./RegistrationReview.sdd
  ./JournalCapacity.sdd
  /contracts/dotnet/LinkGate.Contracts/PendingGrantRequest.sdd
  /docs/adr/0012-pending-grant-requests.md

Must:
  Require actual caller ownership of the explicit application reference and an approved import alias; use uniform authorization errors.
  Capture the approved revision, decision version and normalized import without accepting policy overrides.
  Atomically commit each request and its caller-scoped operation result; replay original results before quota or current-approval checks.
  Retain requests and results without eviction, cap requests per caller at `1024` and globally at `16384`, and preserve revocation reservations.
  Report a request superseded when its captured approval no longer matches, without creating grants, credentials or data flows.
  Keep host enumeration separate from caller-filtered status and reject corrupt stored records with fixed errors.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify authorization, binding, persistence, quotas, rollback, concurrency and RPC/SDK recovery.
